   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">After going around in circles for quite a while, I decided that I needed to ask you all about this example.  The scale_color_manual is being ignored.  What am I doing wrong?  Thanks, Bryan<div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:13.1px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(4,51,255)\">p<span style=\"color:#071a99\"> &lt;- qplot(</span>x <span style=\"color:#071a99\">= </span>carat<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>data <span style=\"color:#071a99\">= </span>diamonds<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>geom <span style=\"color:#071a99\">= </span><span style=\"color:#ff2600\">&quot;density&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>fill <span style=\"color:#071a99\">= </span>cut<span style=\"color:#071a99\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:13.1px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(255,38,0)\"><span style=\"color:#0433ff\">p </span><span style=\"color:#071a99\">&lt;- </span><span style=\"color:#0433ff\">p </span><span style=\"color:#071a99\">+ scale_color_manual(</span><span style=\"color:#0433ff\">values </span><span style=\"color:#071a99\">= c(</span>&quot;red&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;green&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;blue&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">,</span> &quot;orange&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;purple&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">), </span><span style=\"color:#0433ff\">labels </span><span style=\"color:#071a99\">= c(</span>&quot;OK&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;Better&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;Average&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">, </span>&quot;Decent&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">,</span> &quot;Fantastic&quot;<span style=\"color:#071a99\">))</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:13.1px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(4,51,255)\">p</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
